From e5808271b02378327e980bcc62789136efeb9aca Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Josh Smith <josh.smith@plooto.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 00:30:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] feat: optional pgvector-backed semantic search

Adds a heading-aware indexer and four MCP tools (semantic-search,
similar-notes, index-status, reindex-note), all registered only when
DATABASE_URL is set. Embeddings come from a local Ollama server; the index
lives in Postgres with pgvector and is rebuildable from the vault.

- src/index/: config, exclusions, chunker, embedder, store, scanner,
  SearchService; src/indexer.ts entrypoint (same image, second container)
- sql/001_schema.sql applied at start with the model's dimension; model and
  dimension recorded in meta, mismatch refuses to run until --reindex
- hybrid retrieval: HNSW cosine + tsvector, reciprocal rank fusion; filters
  on directory, tags, frontmatter type/status
- change detection by stat then sha256, so NFS/SMB mounts without inotify work
- exclusions enforced by path before any read (.obsidian, .trash, Synology
  litter, AppleDouble, .noindex dirs, index: false)
- tests: chunker and exclusions (pure); search end to end, gated on
  TEST_DATABASE_URL with a deterministic fake embedder

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
